2026-06-30 15:30:36,822 - openai._base_client - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'timeout': 300, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-f6f2c425-6707-4620-a1d1-5470ebbe1b2b', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You are an expert SDRF-Proteomics annotator for crosslinking mass spectrometry (XL-MS) datasets.\n\nExtract the following SDRF metadata terms from the provided publication text and/or PRIDE project description.\n\nTERMS TO EXTRACT:\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nterm: disease\nsdrf_column: characteristics[disease]\nontology: EFO:0000408, MONDO, DOID, PATO\ndescription: Disease state of the sample.\ninstructions: For healthy/normal samples use "normal" (PATO:0000461). For diseased\n  samples use MONDO or DOID terms. Return null only if completely unstated.\n  Most XL-MS samples are "normal" unless explicitly studying a disease model.\n\nterm: phenotype\nsdrf_column: characteristics[phenotype]\nontology: EFO:0000651, PATO, EFO\ndescription: Observable characteristics or traits (drug sensitivity, molecular markers,\n  expression phenotypes, environmental responses).\ninstructions: Return null if not stated. This captures how the sample behaves/appears\n  (distinct from disease diagnosis).\n\nterm: treatment\nsdrf_column: characteristics[treatment]\nontology: EFO:0000727, NCIT, EFO\ndescription: Treatment or perturbation applied to the sample (drug, stimulus,\n  environmental stress, growth condition change).\ninstructions: Return null if not stated or not applicable. Examples: "doxycycline\n  treatment", "heat shock", "DMSO vehicle control".\n\nterm: compound\nsdrf_column: characteristics[compound]\nontology: CHEBI:24431, CHEBI, NCIT, EFO\ndescription: Chemical compound or drug applied to the sample.\ninstructions: Use ChEBI if possible. Return null if no compound treatment. Do NOT\n  include the crosslinking reagent here — that goes in comment[cross-linker].\n\nterm: dose\nsdrf_column: characteristics[dose]\nontology: NCIT:C25488\ndescription: Dose or concentration of compound treatment.\npattern: number + unit (e.g. 10 mg/kg, 50 uM, 100 nM, 10 mg/mL)\ninstructions: Return null if no compound treatment or dose not stated.\n\nterm: genetic modification\nsdrf_column: characteristics[genetic modification]\nontology: EFO:0000510, EFO\ndescription: Method of genetic modification (knockout, knockdown, overexpression,\n  transduction). Describes HOW the modification was done.\ninstructions: Return null if not stated.\n\nterm: perturbation\nsdrf_column: characteristics[perturbation]\nontology: PRIDE:0000700\ndescription: Type of perturbation applied (environmental/experimental perturbation).\ninstructions: Return null if not stated or not applicable.\n\nterm: depletion\nsdrf_column: characteristics[depletion]\nontology: PRIDE:0000020\ndescription: Whether abundant protein depletion was performed.\nallowed_values: no depletion, depletion, not applicable\ninstructions: Return "no depletion" if not mentioned. Return "depletion" if\n  high-abundance protein removal is described (e.g. albumin depletion).\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nReturn a single JSON object where each key is the exact sdrf_column string shown above.\nFor each key, return a dict with:\n  "value": the extracted value (string, list, or null)\n  "accession": ontology accession if resolvable, else null\n  "confidence": "high", "medium", or "low"\n  "evidence_quote": short verbatim quote from the text, or null\n  "evidence_location": location in the paper (e.g. "Methods"), or null'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '[TITLE]\nPerTurboID of Plasmofium falciparum cytoadhesion complex\n\n[ABSTRACT]\nIn this project proximity labeling was used to first identify proteins in the close vicinity of the P. falciparum exported kinase FIKK4.1 by fusing it to a biotin ligase. A conditional KO of the exported kinase FIKK4.1 was then generated for two identified targets, PTP4 and Kahrp in a FIKK4.1 conditional KO line. We then measured the proximity proteome of KAHRP and PTPT4 in the presence, and absence of FIKK4.1.\n\n[METHODS]\nNF54 wildtype parasites, used as controls, and FIKK4.1_TurboID parasites were tightly synchronized to a 4-hour window using Percoll. Parasites were grown in triplicate in 200ml biotin-free complete medium and 2ml of blood to at least 10% parasitemia, with each replicate cultured in blood from a different donor. 4-hour biotin pulses were performed at 2 different timepoints (16 to 20hpi or 40 to 44hpi) by adding 100µM D-biotin (bioAPE) to the cultures in a shaking incubator. After biotinylation, iRBCs were washed 5 times in 50ml biotin-free complete medium. iRBCs treated with biotin between 16 and 20hpi were returned to culture in biotin-free complete medium and allowed to reach late schizont stage (44hpi), then harvested by Percoll and washed 5 times with 5 ml PBS. For the investigation of FIKK4.1 interacting partners on the protein level, purified parasites were lysed in 1% SDS in PBS containing protease inhibitors (cOmplete, Roche) on ice for 30 minutes. Samples were further solubilised by sonication with a microtip sonicator on ice for 3 rounds of 30 seconds at an amplitude of 30%. Lysates were then clarified by centrifugation at 15,000 rpm from 30 minutes at 4\uf0b0C. The protein concentration of the samples was then calculated using a BCA protein assay kit (Pierce). Samples were trypsinized and prepared for mass-spectrometry using established methods.   Samples were loaded onto Evotips (according to manufacturer’s instructions). Following a wash with aqueous acidic buffer (0.1% formic acid in water), samples were loaded onto an Evosep One system coupled to an Orbitrap Fusion Lumos (ThermoFisher Scientific).  The Evosep One was fitted with a 15 cm column (PepSep) and a predefined gradient for a 44-minute method was employed.  The Orbitrap Lumos was operated in data-dependent mode (1 second cycle time), acquiring IT HCD MS/MS scans in rapid mode after an OT MS1 survey scan (R=60,000). The MS1 target was 4E5 ions whereas the MS2 target was 1E4 ions. The maximum ion injection time utilized for MS2 scans was 300 ms, the HCD normalized collision energy was set at 32 and the dynamic exclusion was set at 15 seconds.\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17', 'store': True, 'temperature': 0.3}}
